<article class="env-definition" id="03HL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03HL">Definition <span data-tag="03HL">67.4.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $\Delta _{X/Y} : X \to X \times _ Y X$ be the diagonal morphism. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $f$ is <em>separated</em> if $\Delta _{X/Y}$ is a closed immersion. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $f$ is <em>locally separated</em><a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001351233" id="a0001351233-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> if $\Delta _{X/Y}$ is an immersion. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $f$ is <em>quasi-separated</em> if $\Delta _{X/Y}$ is quasi-compact. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>